cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the associated article below.
title: "Integrated fault detection and supervisory compensation for hydronic radiator faults in district-heated buildings"
abstract: >-
  Code, trained detectors and simulation inputs accompanying the article
  "Integrated fault detection and supervisory compensation for hydronic
  radiator faults in district-heated buildings", published in Results in
  Engineering (Elsevier). Three unsupervised anomaly detectors, trained only
  on a fault-free heating season, run inside the EnergyPlus solver through
  the Python API. A signature-based ladder classifies the detected anomaly
  as a stuck-closed valve, a zone-level over-delivery setpoint bias, or a
  system-level supply-temperature setpoint bias, and a supervisory
  controller adjusts the district-heating supply setpoint accordingly within
  the same simulation. The repository covers detector training, the
  in-the-loop runtime, the severity and compensation-parameter sweeps, the
  compound-fault stress tests, and the analysis that produces the reported
  tables.
